STEP 1: THE GATE (ask before opening anything in docs/source/)
================================================================================

Ask these three together:

  1. Is this a client project or a personal one? Work done for someone else
     counts as a client project, paid or not.
  2. Which AI tools will work on it? Propose the default: Claude Code as the main
     tool, with Codex as an optional backup and second opinion. Accept Claude
     Code only, or both.
  3. Client projects only: for EACH of those tools, have the engagement letter,
     NDA, or institutional terms been confirmed to permit processing this
     client's material with it? Answer yes, no, or unconfirmed per tool. Each AI
     vendor clears separately.

Record each tool's status in AGENTS.md (Confidentiality) and in the "AI-vendor
processing cleared" row of project-status.md's Launch checks.
A tool that isn't cleared must not read the client's material in any form: not
`docs/source/`, and not `docs/sot.md` or `memory/`, which are built from it.

Reading a client's documents through an AI tool IS the act this gate controls.
If the project is a client project and the answer for your own vendor is
anything but an explicit yes:
  - do NOT open any file in docs/source/, including kickoff-notes.md, which
    describes the client's work too
  - say so plainly; the status goes into AGENTS.md and project-status.md as
    unconfirmed
  - skip Step 2 and answer every question in Step 3 by interviewing me, using only
    what I choose to tell you. Retyping a document's contents into chat is the
    same disclosure, so don't ask me to.
  - add this to `.claude/settings.json` (merge with what's there):
        "permissions": { "deny": ["Read(/docs/source/**)"] }
    It blocks Claude Code's file tools and common shell reads (`cat`, `head`)
    on the folder, so a later session can't open it by accident. It is a
    backstop, not a substitute for this rule: a bare `grep -r .` isn't covered,
    and Codex has no equivalent setting.
  - add an open item: "When <vendor> is cleared for this client's material:
    remove the docs/source deny rule from .claude/settings.json, read
    docs/source/, write its index, and re-cite docs/sot.md against the
    originals."
  - anything that must be copied verbatim from a document you can't open
    (phase names, acceptance wording, response or payment windows) is written
    as `TODO: verbatim from <document> once cleared (open-items #N)`. Don't
    fill in default phases in its place.

If your own vendor IS cleared but another tool in use is not, set up normally,
and make sure the Confidentiality section in AGENTS.md names the uncleared tool
and what it must not open.

