--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The four shaping questions. Decide each one separately; never infer one from
another. A client project can be unsigned, and a personal project can involve
money.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  A. Client or personal? (from Step 1)
  B. Is there a contract, TOR, SOW, or written proposal defining the work? Where
     is it, and is it signed? If it exists unsigned, setup may continue, but build
     work and sharing the other party's material wait on signature.
  C. Is money tied to acceptance of specific deliverables? If yes, build the
     Milestones section. If no, delete it.
  D. Light or full?
       Light: one codebase, weeks rather than months.
       Full: several phases with separate sign-offs, months of work, or more
       than one codebase.
     Payment doesn't decide size; that is question C's job. A small site paid
     50/50 is light with two milestones. An undecided stack doesn't either: the
     codebase simply waits, at either size (Step 5).
     A governing document that names phases always supplies them, at either
     size. Otherwise light has NO Phases section (the build list, milestones,
     and launch checks carry its progress), and full takes its phases from the
     standard list in the appendix at the end of this prompt, trimmed to what
     the project involves. Full also maps each launch check to its phase.

